<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-actionable-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The exact provider profile selects only work packets that remain actionable in this profile. One-time imported semantic-first bootstrap and foreground-lifecycle construction scopes remain evidence and governing permission/currentness resources, but are not reprojected as concurrent writers; their omission from selectsContract is neither a completion claim nor removal of the semantic-first policy or lifecycle command capability." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-census-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-census-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Partition the complete frozen models.dev provider-route and model denominator, configured V3 routes, public credential names, installed adapters, explicitly tested local agent transports and the finite reviewed legacy provider/model observation set without treating catalogue membership, a key name, historical admission or an executable as current availability or qualification." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-legacy-observations> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-legacy-observations> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep the names-only reviewed V2 denominator in one tracked closed file with exact permissible source content digests and explicit nonclaims. The secret-bearing untracked V2 environment source is never copied or digested; bind only the canonical names-and-reviewed-alias projection and state that disposition explicitly. The file contains the three host transports; Codex gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-5.5 observations; OpenRouter anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6; MiniMax OAuth MiniMax-M3; the direct OpenAI gpt-5.5 unavailability; the unresolved Nous openai/gpt-5.6-sol route; and the antigravity claude-opus-4.6 configured default. Every row is historical-only, excluded and UNQUALIFIED until independently configured and requalified in V3; the file contains no secret values, session identifiers, host paths or live admission authority." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Read only one explicitly selected owner-only untracked environment file; report presence only for the exact configured and reviewed mapped candidate credential-name set, retain every other public catalogue label in named denominators and aliases, and never copy, print, digest, persist or forward a credential value or reveal the selected path." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-runtime-credential-source> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-runtime-credential-source> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Treat a legacy V1/V2 environment file only as a names-only import source. Normal V3 live operations select an owner-only untracked repository-local .env or .usf/home projection containing only the exact allowlisted variables for the selected route; never copy, graph, digest or persist secret values." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep requested route, provider, route model, underlying family and model, adapter, credential name and host transport identity distinct; preserve unknown rather than guessing aliases." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-account-tier> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before provider inference, use one separately authorized provider-owned non-inference account source to admit a trusted current exact-account tier receipt proving zero paid cost, paid usage disabled, automatic overage disabled, bounded quota applicability and source authenticity; self-authored assertions, promotional credit and model prose are insufficient." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-adapter-preflight> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-adapter-preflight> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Content-verify the exact installed adapter artifact and launch it in a scrubbed child that receives only the selected credential variable, fixed origin, zero-paid ceiling, bounded tokens, timeout and no fallback before provider contact." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-authenticated-answer> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-authenticated-answer> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Acquire provider-produced answers only after current receipt and adapter gates, recording requested and actual identity, sanitized usage, quota, latency, service tier and zero-paid evidence without persisting secrets or full private transcripts." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-hidden-holdout> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-hidden-holdout> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Evaluate genuine hidden holdout cases unavailable to the answer-producing route and bind the exact provider, model, adapter, auth mode, prompt, tool, context, output, suite, corpus and policy versions; default every unmatched or missing answer to UNQUALIFIED." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-routing> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-routing> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Route purely from exact current census, economics, probe and task-profile qualification facts; consider every configured route, explain every exclusion, enforce finite host and provider concurrency, and prohibit paid or unknown fallback." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-parallelism> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-parallelism> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Demonstrate overlapping useful work from at least two independently qualified provider families under bounded provider and host concurrency, without a Docker, GitHub, global mutation-lock or single-composer serialization bottleneck." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
