<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-lazy-fair-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Qualify only current uncovered task roles through deterministic bounded cheapest-first cohorts, count each exact model identity at most once per authorization, reconcile uncertain reservations before retry, fairly drain eligible provider queues across repeated bounded runs, and retain an explicit terminal disposition for every configured identity." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-response-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-response-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Bind requested and actual provider, route, model, adapter and transport identities on every response; a missing, substituted, ambiguous or unauthorized actual identity stops that route after the first response and can never fall back to a requested or default identity." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-cache-exactness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-pipeline-cache-exactness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Key reusable prompt and result state by exact canonical provider, model, transport, semantic prefix, prompt bytes, tools, schemas, model options, context, output and policy; labels alone never alias entries, variable packet suffixes do not corrupt a stable prefix, and unknown or subthreshold provider cache behavior never authorizes a warm chain." <urn:usf:graph:provider-pipeline> .
